":{"zh":"有五根横脊的礼冠，朝中官员最常见的冠帽之一，多在诸侯朝服时佩戴。","en":"A formal cap with five horizontal ridges, one of the most common caps among court officials, typically worn by lords with their court attire."},"defenceVal":"3","mp":"930","price":"4000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1028615","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI107715","name":{"zh":"高阳许氏","en":"The Xu clan of Gaoyang"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"冀州高阳郡高阳县\t出自炎帝之后。秦末高士许猗避乱迁居高阳新城，开基立业。汉魏时期世代为官，为冀州名门。曹魏名士家族。许据官至大司农（九卿），许允官至中领军（典掌禁军），与李丰、夏侯玄友善，谋诛司马师事败被流放。高阳许氏在曹魏中后期拥有重要政治地位。","en":"Gaoyang County, Gaoyang Commandery, Ji Province\tDescendants of the Flame Emperor. At the end of the Qin dynasty, the recluse Xu Yi fled turmoil and settled in Xincheng of Gaoyang, founding the clan's lineage. During the Han and Wei dynasties, generations served as officials, making them a renowned clan of Ji Province and a prominent Family of Cao Wei scholars. Xu Ju rose to Minister of Finance (one of the Nine Ministers), while Xu Yun became Central Commander of the Guard (commanding the imperial guards). Xu Yun was close friends with Li Feng and Xiahou Xuan, after their failed plot to eliminate Sima Shi, he was Exiled. The Xu clan of Gaoyang held significant political influence in the mid-to-late Cao Wei period."},"talent":{"military":"5","commerce":"4","politics":"3"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"许据","height":"较矮","shape":"一般"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":"WJ10072","city":"CS1029","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[45,22,68,67,62,66],"title":28,"rank":"3","loyalty":"98","reputation":"1500","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007102","armor":"WP1015805","helmet":"WP1024905"},"couple":[]},{"story"